WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.251 --> 00:00:19.919
"I think our history teacher is actually making history," Jonathan joked to Carlos.

2
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:28.154
They were walking down the school hallway on Wednesday afternoon. "As the most boring teacher ever!"

3
00:00:28.155 --> 00:00:32.409
Carlos nodded. "I almost fell asleep in class today."

4
00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:38.090
"Me too," Jonathan said. "And I almost threw up my lunch from the school cafeteria.

5
00:00:38.091 --> 00:00:43.156
If I suddenly fall down dead, blame that weird-smelling cheese-and-bean thing I ate."

6
00:00:43.157 --> 00:00:47.646
Carlos grinned. "Okay. Just don't throw up on me!"

7
00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:52.804
"I'll try not to," Jonathan said, laughing. "What a lousy day."

8
00:00:52.805 --> 00:00:59.993
"Look on the bright side," Carlos pointed out. "School's over for the day. Things can only get better for you."

9
00:00:59.994 --> 00:01:03.465
"Hey, guys," someone behind them said.

10
00:01:03.466 --> 00:01:09.474
Jonathan and Carlos turned around. Things had only gotten worse, not better.

11
00:01:09.475 --> 00:01:15.546
Max was walking down the hallway behind them, carrying a soccer ball.

12
00:01:15.547 --> 00:01:17.953
"Hey, Max," Jonathan muttered.

13
00:01:17.954 --> 00:01:21.771
Carlos nodded. "Hey. How's it going?"

14
00:01:21.772 --> 00:01:27.302
"Good. I'm going to practice my soccer skills at the park across the street," Max said.

15
00:01:27.303 --> 00:01:29.876
"Do you guys want to kick the ball around with me?"

16
00:01:29.877 --> 00:01:32.486
"Sure," Carlos said.

17
00:01:32.487 --> 00:01:35.441
"Will your dad be there?" Jonathan asked.

18
00:01:35.442 --> 00:01:38.044
Max shook his head. "Nope."

19
00:01:38.045 --> 00:01:44.438
That was a relief. In Jonathan's opinion, the only person worse than Max was Max's dad.

20
00:01:44.439 --> 00:01:48.758
"Okay," Jonathan said. Carlos was going.

21
00:01:48.759 --> 00:01:52.574
And Jonathan figured that he could leave the park if Max got too annoying.

22
00:01:52.575 --> 00:01:56.262
"Great!" Max sounded surprisingly friendly.

23
00:01:56.264 --> 00:01:59.173
Max surprised Jonathan again at the park.

24
00:01:59.174 --> 00:02:04.471
He took turns kicking the ball with Jonathan and Carlos.

25
00:02:04.472 --> 00:02:09.251
And he didn't brag about being a better player than they were, though clearly he was.

26
00:02:09.252 --> 00:02:17.757
While they practiced soccer passes, Jonathan told one of his favorite jokes. "Hey, Max. Why did Cinderella get chosen last for the soccer team?"

27
00:02:17.758 --> 00:02:21.610
"Huh?" Max said. "I have no idea."

28
00:02:21.611 --> 00:02:25.903
"Because she ran away from the ball!" Jonathan laughed.

29
00:02:25.904 --> 00:02:32.708
Carlos laughed too, even though he'd heard the joke a million times before. But Max just shrugged.

30
00:02:32.709 --> 00:02:38.876
"Max really has no sense of humor," Jonathan thought. It wasn't the first time he'd noticed this.

31
00:02:38.877 --> 00:02:42.049
But other than that, Max seemed pretty cool today.

32
00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:49.889
"Have you seen Lionel Messi do this double fake?" Max asked. He stopped the ball between his feet.

33
00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:53.301
Then he lifted his right foot and took a quick step to the right.

34
00:02:53.302 --> 00:02:58.470
But he dribbled the ball to the left.

35
00:02:58.471 --> 00:03:07.471
"Good one!" Carlos said. "I see why it's called a double fake. You lift your foot and step the opposite way from where you're really going."

36
00:03:07.472 --> 00:03:10.292
Max nodded. "Right."

37
00:03:10.293 --> 00:03:14.291
"That's a cool move," Carlos said.

38
00:03:14.292 --> 00:03:22.681
"When Messi does it, it's amazing. I'll never be as good as he is, but I definitely like practicing his moves," Max said.

39
00:03:22.682 --> 00:03:26.184
"And maybe I can get a soccer scholarship for college."

40
00:03:26.185 --> 00:03:31.274
Jonathan tried the double fake, but he couldn't do it.

41
00:03:31.275 --> 00:03:35.306
"Max, can you show us that in slow motion?" he asked.

42
00:03:35.307 --> 00:03:41.690
"Sure." Max demonstrated the double fake again.

43
00:03:41.691 --> 00:03:44.325
Then he helped Jonathan and Carlos practice it.

44
00:03:44.326 --> 00:03:50.679
"This is awesome," Jonathan said. It was the first new thing he'd learned since joining his team.

45
00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:53.469
Next Max did what he called the hip fake.

46
00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:59.521
He turned his entire body to the right and looked to the right too, as if he'd found a teammate to pass the ball to.

47
00:03:59.522 --> 00:04:05.840
Then he quickly turned his body to the left and kicked the ball left.

48
00:04:05.841 --> 00:04:09.253
"You have a ton of talent," Carlos said.

49
00:04:09.254 --> 00:04:13.493
"Thanks, but really I just work hard," Max said.

50
00:04:13.494 --> 00:04:21.398
"Max is so different today," Jonathan thought. It was as if a nice, humble space alien had secretly taken over Max's body.

51
00:04:21.399 --> 00:04:25.303
Or maybe Max acted like a jerk only when his father was around.

52
00:04:25.304 --> 00:04:31.723
Jonathan looked at him. "Hey, Max. Do you like having your dad coach you?" he asked.

53
00:04:31.724 --> 00:04:36.236
Max frowned. "He definitely helps me improve my game."

54
00:04:36.237 --> 00:04:43.782
"I wish he'd help everyone improve their game," Jonathan blurted out. "But we can't improve if we pass the ball to you all the time.

55
00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:48.137
Why don't you ask your dad to let the rest of the team have the ball more?"

56
00:04:48.138 --> 00:04:50.411
Max crossed his arms.

57
00:04:50.412 --> 00:04:57.034
"My father is the coach and he makes the rules. Instead of complaining, you should take soccer more seriously and practice more."

58
00:04:57.035 --> 00:05:03.295
Jonathan crossed his arms too. "Practice passing the ball to you? No thanks."

59
00:05:03.296 --> 00:05:11.439
"Uh . . ." Carlos looked from Jonathan to Max. "We should probably go, Jonathan. See you later, Max."

60
00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:17.200
"Bye," Max said, dribbling the ball away from them.

61
00:05:17.201 --> 00:05:22.761
Jonathan didn't say anything until he and Carlos were outside the park. "That kid's a jerk."

62
00:05:22.762 --> 00:05:29.012
Carlos shrugged. "He's really good at soccer. Maybe you shouldn't say stuff about his dad."

63
00:05:29.013 --> 00:05:36.599
"Yeah, but . . ." Jonathan was suddenly sick of soccer. He dropped the subject. "See you tomorrow, Carlos."

64
00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:45.745
When Jonathan turned onto his street a few minutes later, he saw Andrew and Aaron shooting a basketball into the hoop on their driveway.

65
00:05:45.746 --> 00:05:51.164
At least they were trying to shoot the ball into the hoop. They were much better at soccer than basketball.

66
00:05:51.165 --> 00:05:56.774
Jonathan joined in.

67
00:05:56.775 --> 00:06:00.808
He wasn't very good at basketball either, but he liked fooling around with the ball.

68
00:06:00.809 --> 00:06:05.051
"What's new?" Andrew asked as he dribbled the ball up the driveway.

69
00:06:05.052 --> 00:06:10.644
"I just hung out with Max Wattenbarger. Now I'm in a bad mood," Jonathan said.

70
00:06:10.645 --> 00:06:19.203
"That would put me in a bad mood too." Andrew took a shot, and the basketball went through the hoop.

71
00:06:19.204 --> 00:06:27.966
Jonathan scooped up the ball. "You should play pro basketball. You could be the next LeBron James, Andrew!" he joked.

72
00:06:27.967 --> 00:06:33.876
"I'm a lot better at soccer. But I'm still glad we quit the soccer team," Andrew said.

73
00:06:33.877 --> 00:06:39.207
"What?" Jonathan was so surprised, he dropped the ball.

74
00:06:39.208 --> 00:06:44.591
It rolled down the driveway and into the gutter.

75
00:06:44.592 --> 00:06:48.939
"We got sick of watching Max hog the ball all the time," Aaron said.

76
00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:51.685
"So we told Coach we were quitting."

77
00:06:51.686 --> 00:06:55.863
"Wow," Jonathan murmured. "That's a bummer."

78
00:06:55.864 --> 00:06:59.173
He liked having the twins on his soccer team.

79
00:06:59.174 --> 00:07:03.197
He went to get the ball and then took a shot.

80
00:07:03.198 --> 00:07:10.264
"You should stay on the team. You're good players. And if we lose you guys, we won't have any substitutes."

81
00:07:10.265 --> 00:07:14.928
"Sorry," Aaron said. "We're done with that team."

82
00:07:14.929 --> 00:07:18.340
"Don't you want to still play soccer?" Jonathan asked.

83
00:07:18.341 --> 00:07:25.516
"The only one who really gets to play is Max Wattenbarger," Andrew said. "The rest of us just pass the ball to him."

84
00:07:25.517 --> 00:07:30.069
"Yeah. No thanks." Aaron threw the basketball to Jonathan.

85
00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:34.082
Jonathan was still distracted by thoughts of playing soccer without the twins.

86
00:07:34.083 --> 00:07:46.294
So he didn't notice the approaching basketball until it hit him. Hard. In his gut.
